      "spam": false,
      "value": "Also I just tested whether triangle count actually matters by profiling a scene with copies of my avatar in it. The full poly (undecimated) avatar is 28k triangles with 1 skinned mesh renderer and 4 materials (4 draw calls).\n\nWith 81 copies of my avatar in frame CPU drawing took ~0.6ms, enabling shadows on the directional light increased this to ~1ms (4 cascades). Approximately doubling the triangle count to 60k triangles still results in ~0.6ms of drawing time, and ~1ms with directional light shadows. Reducing the triangle could by half (14k triangles) does not reduce the CPU drawing time.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
