  "details": "This is a wee bit complex, but could prove beneficial to large events where the sheer number of complex avatars causes performance issues. Basically, admins (or possibly also room owners) would have the ability to activate a performance-friendly avatar mode that automatically switches everyone from their normal avatar to their performance-friendly backup avatar as long as they are in the instance. Accompanying this system would be the ability for users set this backup avatar from the UI. The backup avatar would be forced to adhere to a much stricter set of rules. For example:\n-One Skinned Mesh Renderer only\n-Standard Shaders Only\n-No animation overrides\n-No animations\n-No cloth physics\n-No dynamic bones\n-No particle systems\n-No lights\nEXTRA NOTE: These are example ideas. If such a system were to be implemented, I would expect the devs to figure which restrictions will actually benefit performance the most.\n\nUsers that do not set a backup avatar will instead be switched to a default avatar (compliant default avatars can be set as the backup avatar). Users can change backup avatars while performance-friendly mode is active, but only to other compliant avatars. Users can set the same avatar as their normal and backup avatar, provided it is compliant with the backup avatar rules.\n\n",
